Subject: [PATCH] Keep only the condition's effects when a dead if-valued store is dropped, and do not commute for a sink the middle set consumes

Base: watr deb62e4 (A write after a block that never falls through is conditional in coalesceLocals).

propagate's round runs forwardPropagate, then sinkSets, then eliminateDeadStores. A pure
single-use value substituted at its sole get leaves its local.set for the dead-store sweep;
sinkSets, running first, lands a later set's tee in that dead value as its first use. When
the dead value is an if, dropEffects keeps the structured form whole under a drop, so the
tee'd condition and its pure arms survive as dead work while the use recomputes the arms.
dropEffects now reduces a dead if whose arms are all discardable to the condition's own
effects: (drop (if (local.tee $c X) (then A) (else B))) with A, B discardable becomes
(local.set $c X), and the next round sinks it into the real use.

commuteForSink swapped a commutative node's operands for two adjacent sets even when the
second set's value reads the first set's local: the first set sinks into the second, not
into the swapped statement, and the swap then blocks the second set's own sink (the tee'd
read lands after the swap's other operand reads it). It skips that pair.

Measured on jz at f43229d2 (stock jz passes present): byte-identical over the 58-case bench
corpus at size/2/3/fast and on the level-2 loop-body ratchet. On the local-pass deletion
candidate (jz's propagateSingleUse/foldSetToTee removed): ratchet 10/10 at baseline in every
category (stock watr: buf +5, nest +539, slice +1960, ring +40, condref +952); corpus size -4,
level 2 -30, level 3 -159, fast -5363 B against main. watr unit 349/2 skip, spec 268/20 skip,
propagate-locals 16/16.

Pins to add (test/propagate-locals.js): a dead (local.set $d (if (local.tee $c X) (then A) (else B)))
with pure arms reduces to (local.set $c X); and (local.set $w L) (local.set $h f($h,$w))
(local.set $h g($h,$w)) fuses into one nested statement with both tees.
